  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 is the dominant RNA encoder (~0.72 vs ~0.51 for scgpt), and with scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer, weighted fusion (0.725) marginally edges out concat (0.721). The image encoder choice is the largest untested axis under the scvi_n200 regime — all strong results so far use imagenet_vit_l, but we have no direct comparison with resnet50. Question: Does swapping imagenet_vit_l for resnet50 (config_042: scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) maintain or improve performance? This is a clean single-variable ablation against the current best (config_039). Why this is the best use of experiment 7: It directly tests whether the image encoder contributes meaningfully when the RNA encoder is already strong, reducing uncertainty about a key design choice. With 3 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out resnet50 early lets us either exploit a broader set of resnet50 configs or lock in imagenet_vit_l and focus remaining budget on subtler refinements (e.g., singleprofile, aggregation variants)."
}

